{
  "schema": "research-public-artifact/v1",
  "concept": "Shared case-alert authorization and sensitive-data minimization",
  "slug": "shared-case-alert-authorization-and-sensitive-data-minimization",
  "canonical_concept_id": "concept:3652b9788bbdfa1293893bda4e5b67e8f2a72e30261981d05a7113e0765b4075",
  "canonical_artifact_sha256": "ed79511c96821b05db1ccf575f33cdb9e5f436d3d6a13b2cbb28cf8869a2eba7",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:da4a66d10388c68f0561bb5308c2ff156c8c7be81c1ac6571439ed9ef81c97c6",
      "text": "The change-event schema can contain fields the subscriber cannot access. Schema membership therefore must not serve as the application\u2019s field authorization allowlist. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/change-data-capture/guide/cdc-security-field.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:5b6d271c98f2bda4ec263cdbc2590df29f28024c8a4479be3045e71efe7f251f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:11c63961619944087a48f530de45a98aaf4738438c8b2849e96e18f1f6511aad",
      "text": "The Open WebUI advisory supplies a concrete cross-product failure example: a JWT revoked by sign-out or back-channel logout could still authenticate new realtime connections. This supports testing realtime revocation separately from HTTP; it is not evidence of a Salesforce vulnerability. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/open-webui/open-webui/security/advisories/GHSA-855v-hq7w-jmjw",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:3441d7a991a18a308b9d209a507de2066f33b41a92d1ac788d25e41cc7e0c40d",
        "ev:78e5d2afcae2be14fcbc20e77f8a279ac55e7b6636ba08104db0f3b1b621d147"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:75f7505657e8617f3c6f33d011a1ff71baa0f313dbe60397a25c9d62e148e743",
      "text": "Security boundary caveat: Salesforce evaluates filter expressions even against fields the subscriber cannot access. Do not treat a matching filtered stream as proof that its predicate fields are authorized for the recipient. This caveat concerns authorization, not filter configuration. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/change-data-capture/guide/cdc-filter-considerations.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:12ee58810871b1c1ec9f3477f8fc96fa189e7a68760473349541c8a26d9e46ac"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:f728986d13ae1653c3c1a0e04e386d84004fb11d842de76921935a9dd93a80e4",
      "text": "Design inference: check each recipient\u2019s Case read access before fan-out and again for alert history and details. Collector visibility alone does not establish recipient authorization: CDC ignores sharing, whereas record sharing normally limits which records a user can view. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/change-data-capture/guide/cdc-security-considerations.html",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/cfpb/salesforce-docs/blob/master/_pages/Record-Level-Sharing.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:261c08e7a38d3395dfdb8e6edfe0685b72e4554f84d7ac16c3ac647cd3131849",
        "ev:5b120c2044653d06ba4799a917f4efdd46e9e3d8da23230a2f41ad94d1a89f2a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:300f8a2b5738bef603603823d708455b44e03d80f9fa91f68f654f46a4f3cd27",
      "text": "CDC checks field permissions for the subscribed user before delivery. In a shared collector, this protects the collector\u2019s subscription; it does not establish the field permissions of each downstream alert recipient. The latter is a design inference requiring a separate recipient policy. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/change-data-capture/guide/cdc-security-field.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:5b6d271c98f2bda4ec263cdbc2590df29f28024c8a4479be3045e71efe7f251f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:6ee42aa33cc6454af50de8417c6636852eaed02cf29a59d4095880af50383e10",
      "text": "Design recommendation by analogy to Apache Superset\u2019s notification policy: put only context-free change nudges on a shared broadcast scope; keep Case text and sensitive state out of that scope. Superset expressly prohibits sensitive or authoritative broadcast state. This is supporting engineering precedent, not a Salesforce guarantee. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/apache/superset/blob/master/SECURITY.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:d87c1a9d59599b2e5ac6c6637128a812078f5933cbc5383ef29f04012414032f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:2ba5db64e78ca99638bfabcc87281bb3061b4c71033b9569d7fb424b98943856",
      "text": "For long-lived alert connections, revalidate authorization beyond connection establishment and handle session expiry. OWASP requires closing expired-session sockets; the WebSocket authentication guide warns against trusting a handshake indefinitely. Apply this principle to recipient access changes as a design requirement. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/OWASP/CheatSheetSeries/blob/master/cheatsheets/WebSocket_Security_Cheat_Sheet.md",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/mattheworiordan/websocket.org/blob/main/src/content/docs/guides/authentication.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:0c4e438209aa272456d3df6f052af69b06ef38909f2b6a0a7efa5299b0aeeb0d",
        "ev:ae0f3c10258234fd2a22a3c728f9396063b67fda27e4c554ed333ab356e36450"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:d846e3a8a03de1ff0a2e8f1991173adacf9b9828945f3e73166aa13792e5f303",
      "text": "For the alert service, redact message payloads and credentials from logs. OWASP\u2019s WebSocket guidance explicitly excludes complete messages, authentication tokens, session IDs, and personal information from logging. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/OWASP/CheatSheetSeries/blob/master/cheatsheets/WebSocket_Security_Cheat_Sheet.md",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:43a7f4c167f002c9084f68c506613208fb9bc04308158d1b4e62dd22b4244db4"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "narrative": [
    {
      "assertionId": "prose:bebe962eb9b9bad9b613ce9a3699b03807c0ca518e270a3b05a35d8830740db5",
      "statementSha256": "bebe962eb9b9bad9b613ce9a3699b03807c0ca518e270a3b05a35d8830740db5",
      "assertionKind": "summary",
      "index": 0,
      "documentSlug": "shared-case-alert-authorization-and-sensitive-data-minimization",
      "documentConcept": "Shared case-alert authorization and sensitive-data minimization",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:3652b9788bbdfa1293893bda4e5b67e8f2a72e30261981d05a7113e0765b4075",
      "text": "Shared Case alerting needs recipient authorization beyond collector access. Salesforce CDC ignores record sharing while checking the subscribed user\u2019s field permissions; event schemas can expose field names beyond those permissions. The proposed alert service should check each recipient\u2019s Case access before fan-out and when reading alert history or details. Apache Superset provides a useful precedent for keeping shared broadcasts free of sensitive state. OWASP and a realtime revocation advisory support separate handling of long-lived connection expiry, authorization, and payload redaction. These application design recommendations are distinguished from documented Salesforce behavior.",
